> What do #overview and #annotate do?
They display an overview about the dungeon branches, and let you make
annotations to levels (like, i called level 5 a bone level). The patch
also collects information about temples, shops, fountains, altars and
such stuff automatically (only the ones you've already discovered).
It's very usefull for, for example, remembering where your spellbooks
are (#annotate the level "cancellation spellbook" or so).

